{
  "id": "T18_31_an_expectations_own_interpretation_governs_its_recorded_fulfillment",
  "family": "T18",
  "rules": [
    "7.6.13",
    "7.6.14",
    "7.6.5",
    "7.3.8",
    "6.5.1",
    "9.3.1",
    "9.3.2",
    "9.5.7",
    "4.1.1"
  ],
  "description": "An expectation context may name an interpretation; recorded fulfillment uses it at every instant, and the fulfillment end act carries it. A read under that interpretation, and a read naming none, read the recorded transitions: Door 101's requirement is fulfilled on Tuesday, with act names, and open work and what remains never list it. A normalization of the project, effective Friday, puts the fire-rating interpretation in force for an expectation whose context names none: its \"1.5 h\" evidence of Tuesday now meets the requirement, from Friday only, and the end act cites the normalization in matched_by. The context-named expectation is untouched and keeps its Tuesday fulfillment, with no matched_by. A Wednesday read of the other expectation under its own interpretation is still outstanding; a read naming fire-rating computes under it at every instant. The normalization's exact read has no event_time.",
  "note": "7.6.14: a read \"evaluates an expectation under its own when its frame names no interpretation, whether the expectation's context names one or not, or when its frame names the interpretation that the expectation's context names.\" 7.6.13: \"An expectation's interpretation is the one its context names, at every instant, and no normalization changes it.\" 9.5.7: \"A frame that names no interpretation reads every unit under its own interpretation, so it never lists as outstanding a property that is fulfilled under its own (7.6.13).\" So steps 9, 13, 15 and 23 read door-101|e-fr-i|a-601 from its recorded acts, fulfilled on Tuesday; they do not compute it under the interpretation in force, under which it would be outstanding until Friday's normalization and fulfilled from then with matched_by. 6.5.1: for the other expectation, the qualifying moment is the latest of the evidence's occurrence time, the establishment time \"and, for evidence that meets the value requirement only under an interpretation that a normalization put in force (7.3.8), the instant from which that interpretation is in force for the subject\".",
